# 120 FPS Map, Riverpod & Socket Architecture

## 1. Isolate `GoogleMap` from Parent Rebuilds
- NEVER instantiate `GoogleMap` directly inside `HomeMapPage.build`, `ServiceRequestPage.build`, or `LiveTrackingPage.build` alongside UI overlays.
- Extract the map into a dedicated `RepaintBoundary` + `ConsumerStatefulWidget` (`RyvoMapCanvas`) that ONLY listens to marker sets, polylines, and camera target bounds via `.select()`.
- UI overlays (headers, bottom sheets, bid lists, profile/notification badges) must live in separate sibling `ConsumerWidget` classes inside the `Stack` so state changes never trigger `GoogleMap` rebuilds.

## 2. Granular Riverpod `.select()` Mandate
- NEVER write `ref.watch(jobDraftProvider)` at the root of a screen.
- Always select the exact field required:
  `final pickup = ref.watch(jobDraftProvider.select((s) => s.pickupLocation));`
- Split bloated providers out of `lib/shared/providers/app_providers.dart` into domain-scoped providers when refactoring a feature.

## 3. Smooth 60-120Hz Driver Marker Interpolation
- When `trackingSocketProvider` emits `job:location`, do NOT just jump the marker with raw `setState` on the page.
- Interpolate driver marker `LatLng` and `rotation` (bearing) smoothly over `800ms` using an `AnimationController` inside the isolated Map widget, and eliminate redundant 4-second REST polling whenever the socket connection is active and healthy.